<figure class="work" data-r47-work aria-labelledby="r47-title">
<figcaption id="r47-title"><span>Figure 1</span> The same ten rows, with less work before them</figcaption>
<label>Access path <select data-path><option value="customer">Customer only</option><option value="history">Customer and ordered date</option><option value="cover">Ordered date, with stored status</option></select></label>
<div class="stages"><div><p class="panel-title">Secondary scan</p><p data-scan>60 entries for customer 42</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><p class="panel-title">Primary fetch</p><p data-fetch>60 rows to obtain date and status</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><p class="panel-title">Finish</p><p data-finish>Filter to 15; top-k returns 10</p></div></div>
<p class="total" data-total aria-live="polite">120 decoded KV rows · 2 KV calls</p><p data-reason>The date is unavailable in this secondary index, so all 60 primary rows are fetched before filtering and ordering.</p>
<p class="caption">Redrawn from the recorded CockroachDB 25.4.17 plans, not a live query. One generated table, one local node, identical ten-row answers. Counts describe this run; arrows show data flow, not packet counts or elapsed time. “Primary fetch” is the plan’s index join.</p>
</figure>
<script>
const root=document.querySelector('[data-r47-work]');
if(root){const select=root.querySelector('[data-path]') as HTMLSelectElement;const states={customer:['60 entries for customer 42','60 rows to obtain date and status','Filter to 15; top-k returns 10','120 decoded KV rows · 2 KV calls','The date is unavailable in this secondary index, so all 60 primary rows are fetched before filtering and ordering.'],history:['10 entries in the required order','10 rows to obtain status','Return the ordered 10','20 decoded KV rows · 2 KV calls','The date predicate and order now belong to the secondary scan. Its limit stops after 10 entries, but status still requires primary rows.'],cover:['10 entries, including status','No primary fetch','Return the ordered 10','10 decoded KV rows · 1 KV call','STORING(status) supplies the remaining selected value. The index join disappears; status changes must also maintain this index.']};const draw=()=>{const v=states[select.value];['scan','fetch','finish','total','reason'].forEach((k,i)=>root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`).textContent=v[i]);};select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();}
</script>
<style>
.work{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:.8rem}select{font:inherit;min-width:0;max-width:100%;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.5rem}.stages{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:stretch;gap:.5rem;margin-top:1rem}.stages>div{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.stages>span{align-self:center}.stages p{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:.6rem 0 0}.stages .panel-title{font-weight:600;margin:0}.work .total{border-bottom:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.8rem 0;font:600 .95rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:0}[data-reason]{font:.9rem/1.6 var(--font-sans)}.caption{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){label{display:grid;gap:.4rem}.stages{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stages>span{justify-self:center;transform:rotate(90deg)}}
</style>
